{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067482-mummy-the-resurrection-thread-we-are-the-undying-we-are-eternal","id":1067482,"title":"Mummy The Resurrection Thread: We Are the Undying. We are Eternal.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-24T03:53:32-07:00","id":1067482,"title":"Mummy The Resurrection Thread: We Are the Undying. We are Eternal.","content":"I just bought and read the hardback of Mummy The Resurrection. It's one of my favourite WoD books now, and I couldn't find a Mummy Thread to match the Demon Thread. A few concepts to get the ball rolling;<br /> <br /> - Mummy is interesting since it bridges Cainite, Wraith and Kuei Jin Lore, making them good for crossovers. Has anyone used Mummy allies or antagonists?<br /> <br /> - Mummies are unusual PCs as they are quite high concept. Has anyone played an all Mummy game?<br /> <br /> - Should Necromancy work on the spiritual aspect of a Mummy? It is effectively a Wraith with a fully integrated soul (no Shadow) and a body. Should they be more resistant to Necromancy, since it wasn't designed to control Mummies, but Wraiths?<br /> <br /> - Has a Mummy actually ever died in any of your Games/Stories? Why? I like the idea of a Mage erasing one from the Tapestry, but the backlash from the action unwillingly turns them into a Lich as a fitting response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:25:32-07:00","id":1070184,"title":"","content":"I'm wishing I could play a Mummy game at least once. They look like fun. I had a mummy ally in a game that died before its first session.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mummies are exactly wraiths in a body. I could be wrong. I only have access to the first edition book and haven't read all of it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T10:30:43-07:00","id":1070186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067482-mummy-the-resurrection-thread-we-are-the-undying-we-are-eternal?p=1070184#post1070184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wishing I could play a Mummy game at least once. They look like fun. I had a mummy ally in a game that died before its first session.<br /> <br /> I don't think Mummies are exactly wraiths in a body. I could be wrong. I only have access to the first edition book and haven't read all of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dead Soul + Dead Body = Risen.<br /> <br /> Dead Soul = Wraith.<br /> <br /> Dead Soul fused with Living Soul + Living Body = Mummy.<br /> <br /> You see in Mummy a person almost dies, and their soul is damaged by that and becomes like a Wraith's, fractured Shadow and Ego with scars. And the remnant of a soul from Ancient Egypt is used to glue the soul back together and restore the body to life. Duat is a portion of the shadowlands, and the Mummies are related to Wraiths.<br /> <br /> Mummies as allies are odd. I can see Setites having a Bane Mummy as an Ally, I can see Children of Osiris having Mummy Allies (those are canon), I can see a Mummy jiving with the Anarchs certainly, or even the Camarilla (anything to beat the Tzimisce and Lasombra who embody apothosis far more than the Camarilla clans).<br /> <br /> As for a Mummy game, I like the idea of playing in one, especially since with Level 5 in the Weather power you can make the entire world's cloud layer shift &quot;outrageously&quot; as a Difficulty 8 roll haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 03-29-2017, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T11:30:57-07:00","id":1070212,"title":"","content":"Reading the process of becoming a mummy (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection</a>)<br /> <br /> The mummy is a walking corpse with a wraith and an additional soul in it before the Spell of Life is performed, after which, I think it becomes truly alive and whole once more and not just merely some dead soul and another soul in a living body. That's the whole point of the spell I think. So, after the spell of life is used, I believe that necromancy would be only as effective on it as it would be on a regular person.<br /> <br /> As for a Mummy being a weird ally, I was supposed to play a Bastet, Bubasti.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T11:47:07-07:00","id":1070214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067482-mummy-the-resurrection-thread-we-are-the-undying-we-are-eternal?p=1070212#post1070212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the process of becoming a mummy (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mummy:_The_Resurrection</a>)<br /> <br /> The mummy is a walking corpse with a wraith and an additional soul in it before the Spell of Life is performed, after which, I think it becomes truly alive and whole once more and not just merely some dead soul and another soul in a living body. That's the whole point of the spell I think. So, after the spell of life is used, I believe that necromancy would be only as effective on it as it would be on a regular person.<br /> <br /> As for a Mummy being a weird ally, I was supposed to play a Bastet, Bubasti.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair, and I guess the same is true of Mummy souls in Duat, since they're living souls travelling through the underworld. Necromancy can't attack users of Auspex and Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T13:24:34-07:00","id":1070262,"title":"","content":"I have no real clue of the difference between a living soul and a dead one though.<br /> <br /> My Bastet and the Mummy were supposed to be a bizarre detective duo. I have no idea how that would have worked, really.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mummy games I would like to run:<br /> <br /> One focused on the war with Apophis and the vampires. I guess a bit like Underworld (Movie) with Mummies instead of werewolves or Blade (Movie) with Mummies.<br /> <br /> A ridiculous blend of Mummy and Armageddon (the movie) where a supernatural version of 99942 Apophis is about to hit the earth.<br /> <br /> Some sort of mummy vs mummy conflict. No story for that one yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T14:44:49-07:00","id":1070311,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12480_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12480\" data-vbnamecard=\"12480\">Spacecat</a> Well a living soul is one that hasn't died. A dead soul is one scarred by the very process of dying. A Mage using Spirit to astral project is a Living Soul, the bit of a Silver Fang which turns them into a wolf is a living spirit from Wolf, a Vampire's soul is dead-dead-dead. They died during the embrace, no avoiding that, and this is their dying moments extended into eternity. Borrowed time.<br /> <br /> With Mummy a Dying Soul is repaired using the leftover energy of an old Dead Soul to make a Living Soul which is MORE than most. Sex is better. Food is more flavourful. Music is more sweet. Emotions are stronger.<br /> <br /> This does raise the question; why can't Necromancy control Vampires? My answer is that Necromancy was developed to effect Wraiths (and related groups like Specters), not Dead Souls in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-29T16:03:00-07:00","id":1070364,"title":"","content":"I suppose a necromancy-like discipline could possibly be used to control dead souls in bodies... like maybe zombies, KotE, and Vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T00:31:51-07:00","id":1070515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spacecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1067482-mummy-the-resurrection-thread-we-are-the-undying-we-are-eternal?p=1070364#post1070364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose a necromancy-like discipline could possibly be used to control dead souls in bodies... like maybe zombies, KotE, and Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works on any physical body containing a dead soul. Astrally projected Vampires, Wraiths, no dice. Vampires, Kuei Jin, people possessed by Vampires, people possessed by Wraiths, Risen...<br /> <br /> 1: See if a body you're looking at contains a Dead Soul.<br /> <br /> 2: Lash out mentally and drain the spirit of the soul. Roll Manipulation + Intimidation difficulty of the target's Permanent Willpower, each success removes a point of temporary Willpower, but this is painful and will alert the target to the fact that they are being attacked.<br /> <br /> 3: A dead soul can be compelled to obey. This works on all Vampires and Kuei Jin regardless of Generation or Dharma, but it requires that the user have part of the target's form (some hair, some skin, some blood). Otherwise works as the level 1 Dominate power.<br /> <br /> 4: With a touch, the connection between the Dead Soul and its container may be weakened, inflicting horrific damage. Possessed individuals may be freed, Risen, Vampires and Kuei Jin may be destroyed. Roll Intelligence + Occult, difficulty 6. Each success inflicts a point of Aggravated damage which damages the body through weakening the soul/body bond. Against a possessed individual, 5 successes (may be cumulative) are enough to force the Dead Soul out of them. This power requires contact, and therefore may require a Brawl roll. The target may soak this damage with their Fortitude (or equivalent) if they possess it.<br /> <br /> 5: Dead souls may be manipulated further. With a body sample the user can gain the effects of Dominate 2 and 3, and Presence 4 against a target, regardless of Generation. Any other defenses against these powers may still apply at storyteller discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-30T03:36:04-07:00","id":1070551,"title":"","content":"That sounds like it fits right in. <br /> <br /> I think it would be fun set a Vampire game in Las Vegas with a few Mummies as antagonists. I'm thinking one mummy would be a subtle manipulator with deep pockets, the other would be the kind of crazy magic user who wants to take over the Luxor and rain magical death upon the kindred, and the last is the only one keeping the group together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}